          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bob has three black pens, three blue pens, three red pens and three green pens.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p14-q20-task",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How many ways can he arrange his pens in a row so that no two adjacent pens are the same colour?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "41\\,304",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " arrangements.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use inclusion–exclusion, grouping adjacent identical pens into blocks and correcting for overlapping groups.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-worked-total",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Pens of the same colour are identical. Without restrictions, the number of arrangements is ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{12!}{(3!)^4}=369\\,600",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-worked-bonds",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For each colour, consider its three occurrences in left-to-right order. There are two possible adjacency bonds: between the first and second occurrences, and between the second and third. Select bonds and merge the joined pens into single blocks. Inclusion–exclusion subtracts selections of one bond, adds selections of two bonds, and continues with alternating signs.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-worked-cases",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let a colours have one selected bond, b colours have both bonds selected, and c colours have none. Then ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a+b+c=4,\\qquad j=a+2b",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". There are ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{4!}{a!b!c!}2^a",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " bond selections of this type. After merging, there are ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "12-j",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " blocks. Each colour with no selected bond contributes three identical singleton blocks. For a colour with one selected bond, the pair-block must precede the singleton when the first bond is selected, and must follow it when the second bond is selected. Only one of their two possible orders is allowed for each selection, so divide by 2! for each of these a colours.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-worked-term-definition",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "T_j",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " be the total count over all selections of j bonds. Thus",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "T_j=\\sum_{\\substack{a,b,c\\geq0\\\\a+b+c=4\\\\a+2b=j}}\\frac{4!\\,2^a(12-j)!}{a!b!c!(2!)^a(3!)^c}.",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q20-worked-first-term",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For example, choosing one of the eight bonds gives",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "T_1=8\\times\\frac{11!}{2!(3!)^3}=739\\,200.",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
